VulkanLumen — reusable Lumen-style lighting interface (SKELETON)

This module deliberately does not render GI yet. record() and compose()
emit no GPU commands; result() contains null VkImage handles; implemented()
returns false. It builds as a standalone VulkanLumen library.

The host controls the Vulkan device, swapchain, render pass, camera and
scene lifetime. VulkanLumen owns its future internal scene representation,
surface cache, screen probes, radiance probes, and reconstruction passes.

Stable public API (lumen/lumen.hpp)
  create(pass, format, extent, settings)
  set_scene(scene) / set_lighting(lighting) / set_gbuffer(gbuffer)
  record(command, frame)              BEFORE the host presentation render pass
  compose(command)                    INSIDE the host presentation render pass
  result()                            future indirect/reflection outputs
  invalidate() / resize(...) / reset()
  implemented()

Demo: settings.demo = demo_scene::cornell_box requests an internally managed
Cornell demonstration once the Lumen implementation is written. Applications
with actual world geometry will supply their own scene and G-buffer instead.

Implementation milestones, all confined to lumen/:
  1. Internal raster visibility or optional external G-buffer
  2. Scene tracing backed by VulkanBVH / SDF tracing as appropriate
  3. Screen tracing and disocclusion fallback
  4. Surface representation and cached surface lighting
  5. Screen probes, radiance cache, visibility-aware probe interpolation
  6. Budgeted updates and invalidation for moving lights/geometry
  7. Diffuse indirect and reflection outputs
  8. Composite into the compatible host render pass
  9. GPU timestamps and M1 low-end quality settings

Shaders/resources are intentionally absent until those passes exist. The
stable API permits vulkan-experiment/main.cpp to remain unchanged when the
implementation is filled in. The host will remain a black, responsive Vulkan
window until the first actual rendering pass is implemented.

Build independently with c build run VulkanLumen from lumen/, or link it as a
c_dep_subdir(...,"lumen") / c_dep_cbuild(...,"VulkanLumen",...) dependency.
